1
00:00:04,482 --> 00:00:07,920
[light acoustic music]

2
00:00:08,878 --> 00:00:10,662
[group gasping]

3
00:00:10,793 --> 00:00:11,837
- It's finally done.

4
00:00:11,968 --> 00:00:14,188
Our new house is complete!

5
00:00:14,318 --> 00:00:16,668
Looking at it now, it is huge.

6
00:00:16,799 --> 00:00:19,323
- Keep on digging deeper!

7
00:00:19,454 --> 00:00:21,064
We're going to add a cellar!

8
00:00:21,195 --> 00:00:22,631
- You want me to keep going?

9
00:00:22,761 --> 00:00:24,981
- We need giant
support beams, too.

10
00:00:25,112 --> 00:00:26,983
- And here comes the swing.

11
00:00:27,114 --> 00:00:28,550
Fore!

12
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:31,422
Yep. I had an inkling it
would turn out like this,

13
00:00:31,553 --> 00:00:32,989
but still.

14
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,383
- And Tia and I helped come up
with the new design.

15
00:00:35,513 --> 00:00:36,210
Right?

16
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,385
- Of course!

17
00:00:37,515 --> 00:00:38,734
We also addressed the requests

18
00:00:38,864 --> 00:00:40,866
of the future residents
while you built.

19
00:00:40,997 --> 00:00:43,304
- I'm a resident too, you know.

20
00:00:43,434 --> 00:00:45,175
- It just wouldn't have
felt right, Hiraku,

21
00:00:45,306 --> 00:00:48,700
if you didn't have
the nicest house here.

22
00:00:48,831 --> 00:00:50,833
Let's tour the interior.

23
00:00:50,963 --> 00:00:51,964
- [Hiraku] Whoa.

24
00:00:54,663 --> 00:00:57,492
Looks a lot like the
house you live in, Lea.

25
00:00:57,622 --> 00:00:59,276
- [Lea] Right now
we're in the main hall.

26
00:00:59,407 --> 00:01:01,496
We designed it so that
everyone could gather here

27
00:01:01,626 --> 00:01:02,671
and hang out.

28
00:01:03,802 --> 00:01:06,196
And Hiraku, this is
your room here.

29
00:01:07,284 --> 00:01:09,156
- Oh.

30
00:01:09,286 --> 00:01:11,027
I like it.

31
00:01:11,158 --> 00:01:14,596
- [Lea] And opposite your room
across the main hall is...

32
00:01:15,423 --> 00:01:16,250
the dining room!

33
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:19,122
- This is impressive.

34
00:01:19,253 --> 00:01:21,385
- [Lea] There's a kitchen
in the back.

35
00:01:21,516 --> 00:01:24,910
We even set up
more stoves outside.

36
00:01:25,041 --> 00:01:27,391
- So this is the cellar, huh?

37
00:01:27,522 --> 00:01:31,134
This will be great for
storing food and firewood.

38
00:01:34,268 --> 00:01:36,183
- [Lu] I was hoping for
my own room!

39
00:01:36,313 --> 00:01:39,229
- It was getting crowded with
all the people we have now.

40
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:41,536
- Looks like you
like your rooms.

41
00:01:41,666 --> 00:01:42,928
- Yeah!

42
00:01:43,059 --> 00:01:45,366
- So what's this room
over here then?

43
00:01:45,496 --> 00:01:48,020
This one has a bolt lock
for some reason.

44
00:01:49,021 --> 00:01:51,198
Why did they put one here?

45
00:01:56,203 --> 00:01:58,205
I'll pretend
I didn't see that.

46
00:01:58,335 --> 00:02:00,163
- It's really exciting
to finally see

47
00:02:00,294 --> 00:02:01,817
your new house like this.

48
00:02:01,947 --> 00:02:04,124
- I love everything about it.

49
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:07,910
[Hiraku laughs]

50
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:09,825
- Looking up at
that tree from here

51
00:02:09,955 --> 00:02:13,437
makes it feel like
it's watching over us.

52
00:02:13,568 --> 00:02:15,222
This house is great, Lea.

53
00:02:15,352 --> 00:02:17,137
- Thank you for saying so.

54
00:02:17,267 --> 00:02:19,139
After you've spent
the winter here,

55
00:02:19,269 --> 00:02:21,750
I want you to tell me if you
feel any of its unsatisfactory,

56
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,055
so that we may fix it.

57
00:02:23,186 --> 00:02:24,579
- As you wish.

58
00:02:24,709 --> 00:02:26,189
There we go.

59
00:02:27,495 --> 00:02:29,758
[Hiraku sighs]

60
00:02:29,888 --> 00:02:31,542
In addition to my God statue,

61
00:02:31,673 --> 00:02:33,936
I decided to make
some statues of my dogs.

62
00:02:34,066 --> 00:02:37,069
I put them in front of the
entrances to the new homes.

63
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,985
Yeah. This is shaping up
pretty nicely.

64
00:02:40,116 --> 00:02:42,945
[light upbeat music]

65
00:02:44,903 --> 00:02:48,080
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

66
00:04:16,081 --> 00:04:17,344
- Hm.

67
00:04:17,474 --> 00:04:20,869
This looks like
all the main ingredients.

68
00:04:20,999 --> 00:04:23,437
- I overdid it out there,
and now I'm starving.

69
00:04:23,567 --> 00:04:25,700
What are we eating
for our meal today?

70
00:04:25,830 --> 00:04:28,006
- I'm going to try and see
if I can manage a new dish

71
00:04:28,137 --> 00:04:29,312
we haven't tried.

72
00:04:29,443 --> 00:04:31,227
- A new dish
we haven't tried yet?

73
00:04:31,358 --> 00:04:34,317
- Yeah. It's a dish
called curry.

74
00:04:34,448 --> 00:04:36,188
- [Lu] Hmm. I've never
heard of that.

75
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:38,278
- You're going to
try to make it?

76
00:04:38,408 --> 00:04:40,018
Then does that mean
that this curry

77
00:04:40,149 --> 00:04:42,107
is a difficult dish
to put together?

78
00:04:42,238 --> 00:04:46,373
- Well, it can be easy, but
mastering it takes some work.

79
00:04:46,503 --> 00:04:50,638
Usually you just add roux
to the pot and be done.

80
00:04:50,768 --> 00:04:52,117
[both gasp]

81
00:04:52,248 --> 00:04:54,206
- So that's the kinda stuff
you're into you?

82
00:04:54,337 --> 00:04:55,295
- You savage!

83
00:04:55,425 --> 00:04:58,385
- What are you talking about?

84
00:04:58,515 --> 00:05:01,431
- Wow. I didn't know you planted
all these crop fields too.

85
00:05:01,562 --> 00:05:03,781
- I've been working at it
bit by bit.

86
00:05:03,912 --> 00:05:06,436
- [Tia] There are a lot of
plants here I don't recognize.

87
00:05:06,567 --> 00:05:08,917
- Yep. That's because there
are a lot of plants here

88
00:05:09,047 --> 00:05:11,702
that normally can't grow
in climates with snowfall.

89
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:13,182
With the almighty farming tool,

90
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:15,140
I can grow plants that
are really sensitive

91
00:05:15,271 --> 00:05:16,577
to seasonal weather.

92
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:20,407
The almighty tool
really does it all.

93
00:05:20,537 --> 00:05:24,933
Okay. Let's harvest the spices
we're gonna need for the curry.

94
00:05:25,063 --> 00:05:26,717
First up is cumin.

95
00:05:26,848 --> 00:05:28,893
- That's a cute sounding
name for a plant.

96
00:05:29,024 --> 00:05:30,895
- It looks already dried out.

97
00:05:31,026 --> 00:05:33,463
- Once the flower blooms,
the seed left behind makes

98
00:05:33,594 --> 00:05:37,685
for a good spice and is most
responsible for curry's aroma.

99
00:05:39,556 --> 00:05:41,993
- What a peculiar smell
this seed has.

100
00:05:42,124 --> 00:05:43,734
- Next up is turmeric.

101
00:05:43,865 --> 00:05:46,084
It's the thing that
gives curry its color.

102
00:05:46,215 --> 00:05:47,912
The part we care about
is the root,

103
00:05:48,043 --> 00:05:50,524
but the part that grows
above ground is pretty huge.

104
00:05:50,654 --> 00:05:53,178
We dry out the root
and use that.

105
00:05:53,309 --> 00:05:54,745
- [Lu And Tia] Dry out, dry out.

106
00:05:54,876 --> 00:05:56,443
- [Hiraku] I ended up
asking the girls

107
00:05:56,573 --> 00:05:57,879
to dry them out for me.

108
00:05:58,009 --> 00:05:59,707
- Become dry, dry out!
- Magic is really handy.

109
00:05:59,837 --> 00:06:01,665
Next, is coriander.

110
00:06:01,796 --> 00:06:06,061
We grind the seeds up
in the powder to use.

111
00:06:06,191 --> 00:06:09,107
- This one has a nice and
fresh fruit-like aroma.

112
00:06:09,238 --> 00:06:15,157
- Yeah. The green leaves up top
are an herb called cilantro.

113
00:06:15,287 --> 00:06:17,638
These always have
a potent aroma.

114
00:06:17,768 --> 00:06:19,466
[wolf barks]

115
00:06:19,596 --> 00:06:20,597
[wolves panting]

116
00:06:20,728 --> 00:06:22,425
You want to eat this?

117
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:29,171
Well, I guess we like
different flavors.

118
00:06:29,301 --> 00:06:31,086
- Did you see that?

119
00:06:31,216 --> 00:06:35,003
- Yeah. That's a plant capable
of driving off inferno wolves.

120
00:06:35,133 --> 00:06:39,224
I think that one will be
worth researching.

121
00:06:39,355 --> 00:06:43,664
- Next we have black pepper
and cayenne peppers.

122
00:06:43,794 --> 00:06:47,145
Great! These are all
the spices I'll need.

123
00:06:47,276 --> 00:06:49,452
Wait, hold on.

124
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,718
I heard that girls think
guys who make their own curry

125
00:06:54,849 --> 00:06:57,155
from scratch are
a pain in the ass.

126
00:06:57,286 --> 00:06:59,462
I wonder if that's really true.

127
00:06:59,593 --> 00:07:02,422
[playful music]

128
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:04,511
All right.

129
00:07:04,641 --> 00:07:06,556
This feels pretty authentic.

130
00:07:07,818 --> 00:07:08,993
By the way.

131
00:07:10,865 --> 00:07:12,693
Are you my only helper, Lea?

132
00:07:12,823 --> 00:07:16,348
- [Lea] Yes. Lu and Tia said
they're busy with research.

133
00:07:16,479 --> 00:07:18,133
They said something about
an all powerful

134
00:07:18,263 --> 00:07:20,657
magical protection talisman?

135
00:07:20,788 --> 00:07:23,791
- [Hiraku] Whatever.
We can handle it together.

136
00:07:23,921 --> 00:07:25,009
- Yes.

137
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:27,751
[playful music]

138
00:07:27,882 --> 00:07:31,276
- First, we start by heating up
rapeseed oil we extracted.

139
00:07:32,626 --> 00:07:35,019
Then we go ahead and
add in the rabbit meat.

140
00:07:35,150 --> 00:07:36,847
- Okay.

141
00:07:36,978 --> 00:07:39,546
- While that's cooking,
we grind up all the spices

142
00:07:39,676 --> 00:07:42,070
except for the cumin
into a powder.

143
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:45,116
- Is this enough for the meat
or does it need more time?

144
00:07:45,247 --> 00:07:46,422
- It looks good.

145
00:07:46,553 --> 00:07:47,858
Once you've got some
color on the meat,

146
00:07:47,989 --> 00:07:50,557
take it off the heat
so it doesn't overcook.

147
00:07:50,687 --> 00:07:52,689
Cook the cumin into
the leftover bits

148
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:56,084
and juices from the meat to
bring out the flavor and aroma.

149
00:07:56,214 --> 00:07:58,565
Be careful not to burn them.

150
00:07:58,695 --> 00:08:01,219
It's already starting to
smell like curry.

151
00:08:01,350 --> 00:08:02,351
- Wow.

152
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:04,005
I've never smelled this before.

153
00:08:04,135 --> 00:08:06,442
- Next, we need to focus on
sauteing the onions,

154
00:08:06,573 --> 00:08:08,009
ginger, and garlic.

155
00:08:08,139 --> 00:08:11,621
Smooth them around like so,
and then saute them

156
00:08:11,752 --> 00:08:13,318
without burning them.

157
00:08:13,449 --> 00:08:16,017
Now we add the diced tomatoes

158
00:08:16,147 --> 00:08:18,193
and keep on sauteing everything.

159
00:08:20,151 --> 00:08:21,849
- [Lea] Would you like
me to stir for a bit?

160
00:08:21,979 --> 00:08:23,546
- [Hiraku] Thanks.

161
00:08:23,677 --> 00:08:26,506
Once it's turned into a
nice paste, we can move on.

162
00:08:26,636 --> 00:08:27,724
Spices in, boom.

163
00:08:27,855 --> 00:08:29,509
We add salt, too.

164
00:08:30,466 --> 00:08:31,772
Cook it a little more.

165
00:08:31,902 --> 00:08:33,948
Then we add in the meat
and boiled soybeans

166
00:08:34,078 --> 00:08:35,297
along with some water.

167
00:08:35,427 --> 00:08:37,255
- It already smells delicious.

168
00:08:37,386 --> 00:08:40,607
- [Hiraku] Now we let it simmer
until the meat gets soft.

169
00:08:42,826 --> 00:08:45,046
- Do we just need to
wait for it now?

170
00:08:45,176 --> 00:08:46,047
- Yeah.

171
00:08:46,177 --> 00:08:47,614
We wait for it to cook.

172
00:08:47,744 --> 00:08:49,746
I feel like I'm forgetting
something though.

173
00:08:49,877 --> 00:08:51,879
What could it be?

174
00:08:52,009 --> 00:08:53,489
[Hiraku gasps]

175
00:08:54,098 --> 00:08:55,012
The naan!

176
00:08:55,143 --> 00:08:55,926
- What is naan?

177
00:08:56,057 --> 00:08:57,101
- It's naan, naan!

178
00:08:57,232 --> 00:08:58,538
- It's naan, naan?

179
00:08:58,668 --> 00:08:59,887
- [Hiraku] I was so focused
on the curry

180
00:09:00,017 --> 00:09:01,845
that I forgot
about it completely.

181
00:09:01,976 --> 00:09:03,804
Should I just make rice?

182
00:09:03,934 --> 00:09:06,110
No. I want naan with this curry.

183
00:09:06,241 --> 00:09:08,460
How many portions
do I need to make?

184
00:09:08,591 --> 00:09:10,941
Me, Lu, Tia.

185
00:09:11,072 --> 00:09:14,554
And if I add the elves, that
makes, well, it makes a lot.

186
00:09:14,684 --> 00:09:17,731
It's the same recipe as bread
right up to where it rises.

187
00:09:17,861 --> 00:09:20,211
The difference is that now
we roll the dough

188
00:09:20,342 --> 00:09:21,604
out with a rolling pin.

189
00:09:21,735 --> 00:09:22,910
- Right.

190
00:09:24,868 --> 00:09:27,001
We're going to cook it now,
right, Hiraku?

191
00:09:27,131 --> 00:09:28,742
- Yeah, that's right.

192
00:09:28,872 --> 00:09:31,745
You're supposed to cook it
inside of the stove.

193
00:09:31,875 --> 00:09:34,182
But I've seen people use
the outside of a pot before,

194
00:09:34,312 --> 00:09:36,750
so we'll try that.

195
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,229
- What an interesting
little plant this herb

196
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,666
turned out to be.

197
00:09:39,796 --> 00:09:41,798
- [Tia] It doesn't appear
to be poisonous.

198
00:09:42,799 --> 00:09:44,671
- [Lu] What are they up to?

199
00:09:44,801 --> 00:09:46,716
- I can smell
something appetizing

200
00:09:46,847 --> 00:09:49,153
coming from over there.

201
00:09:49,284 --> 00:09:52,156
And we haven't eaten yet today.

202
00:09:52,287 --> 00:09:54,071
- Yeah, you're right.

203
00:09:55,638 --> 00:09:57,858
- And here's the last one.

204
00:09:57,988 --> 00:09:59,990
Great. And now for this.

205
00:10:00,121 --> 00:10:02,036
It should be just about
done now.

206
00:10:08,259 --> 00:10:09,696
- This is.

207
00:10:09,826 --> 00:10:11,262
- [Tia] Curry, you said?

208
00:10:11,393 --> 00:10:13,656
- [Lu] It's got a strange
color to it.

209
00:10:13,787 --> 00:10:17,007
- [Tia] I'll need to work up a
little courage to try eating it.

210
00:10:17,138 --> 00:10:20,228
- You don't need to be so shy.

211
00:10:20,358 --> 00:10:23,361
I think it probably came out
pretty well.

212
00:10:23,492 --> 00:10:25,799
You scoop up the curry
with the naan.

213
00:10:25,929 --> 00:10:27,975
That's why it's flat like this.

214
00:10:30,847 --> 00:10:32,109
Mm, it's great.

215
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:33,720
This is actual curry!

216
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:36,810
I can smell all the spices
throughout it.

217
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:45,209
- Oh, my!

218
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:48,343
This spiciness seems like
it could become addicting.

219
00:10:48,473 --> 00:10:51,825
- The ratio of spices you use
changes the flavor, right?

220
00:10:51,955 --> 00:10:54,392
This will definitely be
worth researching.

221
00:10:54,523 --> 00:10:58,135
- Every bite I take makes you
want to eat even more of it.

222
00:10:58,266 --> 00:11:01,573
- I'm so glad to hear you
all enjoyed it so much.

223
00:11:01,704 --> 00:11:03,575
Well, it's got a
pretty unique taste,

224
00:11:03,706 --> 00:11:04,968
so if you don't really like it,

225
00:11:05,099 --> 00:11:07,318
there's no need to force
yourself to eat it.

226
00:11:10,191 --> 00:11:12,454
Hey girls, would you mind
leaving a little curry

227
00:11:12,584 --> 00:11:14,456
and naan for me too, please?

228
00:11:17,241 --> 00:11:19,243
- Wow. It really does work!

229
00:11:19,374 --> 00:11:21,463
- Well is is pretty spicy.

230
00:11:21,593 --> 00:11:24,161
- I'm glad the
customers liked it,

231
00:11:24,292 --> 00:11:25,772
but now I'm sold out.

232
00:11:25,902 --> 00:11:28,339
This isn't the first time
it's happened.

233
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:30,646
- Wow, I'm stuffed.

234
00:11:30,777 --> 00:11:33,431
- I definitely wanna
eat that again soon.

235
00:11:33,562 --> 00:11:35,477
- [Lea] I've pretty much
memorized the recipe.

236
00:11:35,607 --> 00:11:39,611
- [Lu] Let's change up how
much spice we use next time.

237
00:11:39,742 --> 00:11:40,830
- [Hiraku] Well they
all liked it,

238
00:11:40,961 --> 00:11:42,876
so I guess that's
what's important.

239
00:11:43,006 --> 00:11:45,835
But still, eating just
a few bites of curry,

240
00:11:45,966 --> 00:11:47,619
really makes you hungry.

241
00:11:48,577 --> 00:11:49,534
Farming life...

242
00:11:49,665 --> 00:11:50,579
- [Lea] ...In Another...

243
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:51,754
- ...World.

244
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:58,805
This year's winter
started to draw near.

245
00:11:58,935 --> 00:12:00,458
Once the snow starts to fall,

246
00:12:00,589 --> 00:12:03,244
we'll spend most of our days
inside the house.

247
00:12:03,374 --> 00:12:05,115
We'll need to finish
our winter preparations

248
00:12:05,246 --> 00:12:07,901
before that happens.

249
00:12:08,031 --> 00:12:10,425
We should be all right
with this much firewood.

250
00:12:11,252 --> 00:12:13,471
Hey! Zabuton!

251
00:12:13,602 --> 00:12:15,343
I brought you something.

252
00:12:15,473 --> 00:12:17,214
When it gets cold outside,

253
00:12:17,345 --> 00:12:20,043
Zabuton hibernates at
the top of the tree.

254
00:12:22,785 --> 00:12:24,308
Right. That's good.

255
00:12:24,439 --> 00:12:26,876
I made sure to ask for extra
blankets ahead of time.

256
00:12:27,007 --> 00:12:28,269
Thanks again!

257
00:12:28,399 --> 00:12:30,358
We really needed these.

258
00:12:30,488 --> 00:12:32,752
[hammer thudding]

259
00:12:32,882 --> 00:12:35,842
Hey, good work.

260
00:12:35,972 --> 00:12:37,757
- [Lea] You too, good work.

261
00:12:37,887 --> 00:12:40,237
- Lea, along with the elves
are going to keep working

262
00:12:40,368 --> 00:12:43,501
on the forge and some other
projects through the winter.

263
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:49,464
Huh?

264
00:12:49,594 --> 00:12:53,033
I'm having Lu and Tia preserve
some food for the winter.

265
00:12:53,163 --> 00:12:57,385
We season the meat,
then smoke it and dry it.

266
00:12:57,515 --> 00:13:00,214
Kuro and the dogs won't
be able to hunt very well

267
00:13:00,344 --> 00:13:03,043
during the winter
once it starts to snow.

268
00:13:03,173 --> 00:13:06,394
That's why I want to stock up
on as much as possible.

269
00:13:06,524 --> 00:13:08,744
[Tia yells]

270
00:13:08,875 --> 00:13:12,879
Well, I think we'll be okay
as far as meat goes.

271
00:13:13,009 --> 00:13:15,838
Right now, I'm working on a way
to preserve vegetables.

272
00:13:15,969 --> 00:13:19,537
The vegetables go into
the boxes on top.

273
00:13:19,668 --> 00:13:21,235
Then they're covered in a sheet,

274
00:13:21,365 --> 00:13:24,194
and then we cover them
with snow.

275
00:13:24,325 --> 00:13:26,022
It's called snow storage.

276
00:13:26,153 --> 00:13:27,676
The bottom boxes collect water

277
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:29,983
from the snow to keep the
vegetables dry.

278
00:13:30,113 --> 00:13:32,289
I'll try it out
as soon as it snows.

279
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:33,943
- Here I go!

280
00:13:34,074 --> 00:13:37,033
I'm going to burn
all of you to ashes.

281
00:13:37,164 --> 00:13:38,905
- [Tia] You're not
supposed to burn them!

282
00:13:39,035 --> 00:13:40,471
- [Lu] I'm just messing around.

283
00:13:40,602 --> 00:13:42,647
- I wish I could use magic.

284
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:46,913
[Hiraku yells]

285
00:13:47,043 --> 00:13:49,045
Even though I knew it
wouldn't work,

286
00:13:49,176 --> 00:13:51,613
watching them use magic
every day made me feel like

287
00:13:51,743 --> 00:13:54,007
I needed to try it
for some reason.

288
00:13:54,137 --> 00:13:55,617
I wonder why.

289
00:14:01,928 --> 00:14:04,713
- Ignition may be
a low level spell,

290
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:07,759
but you still can't go and use
it without studying magic.

291
00:14:07,890 --> 00:14:10,414
- Yeah, guess you're
right about that.

292
00:14:10,545 --> 00:14:12,025
You all make it look so easy

293
00:14:12,155 --> 00:14:14,723
that I just thought
maybe I could do it too.

294
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:18,379
I tried copying it,
but naturally, it didn't work.

295
00:14:18,509 --> 00:14:20,860
- The golems Tia summons
are difficult to use even

296
00:14:20,990 --> 00:14:22,687
among other magic users.

297
00:14:22,818 --> 00:14:24,864
- [Hiraku] Then doesn't that
mean she's pretty amazing,

298
00:14:24,994 --> 00:14:27,040
since she can summon a
bunch of them at once?

299
00:14:27,170 --> 00:14:31,131
- Well, yeah, but I can do a lot
of cool magic too, you know?

300
00:14:31,261 --> 00:14:34,003
- Of course, I know.

301
00:14:34,134 --> 00:14:36,049
But still, you guys
are all amazing.

302
00:14:36,179 --> 00:14:38,399
I'm glad that I have
you for help.

303
00:14:38,529 --> 00:14:39,661
All I've been doing around here

304
00:14:39,791 --> 00:14:41,663
is some garden work and cooking.

305
00:14:42,969 --> 00:14:44,318
- What are you talking about?

306
00:14:44,448 --> 00:14:46,494
You're the most
amazing one here.

307
00:14:47,364 --> 00:14:49,018
- I am?

308
00:14:49,149 --> 00:14:51,934
- Living out here like this for
as long as you have already,

309
00:14:52,065 --> 00:14:54,894
that's not something
just anyone can do.

310
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,592
- If you say so.

311
00:14:57,722 --> 00:15:01,901
- I do. No one's been able to do
something like this till now.

312
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:03,685
It's just you.

313
00:15:03,815 --> 00:15:05,382
You're the only one that has.

314
00:15:05,513 --> 00:15:07,210
- Really?

315
00:15:07,341 --> 00:15:08,777
- Yep!

316
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:12,824
[light orchestral music]

317
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:28,753
- And so, winter had arrived.

318
00:15:28,884 --> 00:15:31,191
The snow began piling up.

319
00:15:31,321 --> 00:15:34,281
I think that's it.

320
00:15:34,411 --> 00:15:36,370
We were spending
more time indoors,

321
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:38,850
so we needed things
to do for fun.

322
00:15:38,981 --> 00:15:41,592
I started with
a classic, Reversi.

323
00:15:41,723 --> 00:15:46,336
Then I built a chess set,
as well as a Majong set.

324
00:15:48,773 --> 00:15:50,210
- Reversi?

325
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:51,646
- Yeah.

326
00:15:51,776 --> 00:15:53,387
You play the game with
black and white pieces.

327
00:15:53,517 --> 00:15:55,041
When you surround
the opponent's piece

328
00:15:55,171 --> 00:15:56,912
you flip it to your color.

329
00:15:57,043 --> 00:15:58,740
The game ends when
the board is filled

330
00:15:58,870 --> 00:16:01,221
and whoever has
the most pieces wins.

331
00:16:01,351 --> 00:16:02,874
Those are the rules.

332
00:16:03,005 --> 00:16:04,964
- What a simple sounding game.

333
00:16:05,094 --> 00:16:07,140
Is it really all that
fun to play then?

334
00:16:07,270 --> 00:16:08,706
- How shortsighted of you.

335
00:16:08,837 --> 00:16:10,404
It's the simple design
that allows

336
00:16:10,534 --> 00:16:13,363
for complicated strategies
to be developed.

337
00:16:13,494 --> 00:16:15,104
- You're right on.

338
00:16:15,235 --> 00:16:18,151
It's amazing you know that
just from hearing the rules.

339
00:16:18,281 --> 00:16:19,674
- It's nothing.

340
00:16:19,804 --> 00:16:21,067
- Right!

341
00:16:21,197 --> 00:16:23,199
I challenge you
to a game now, Tia.

342
00:16:23,330 --> 00:16:25,288
- If that's what you desire.

343
00:16:25,419 --> 00:16:27,334
After all, we've entered
a temporary truce,

344
00:16:27,464 --> 00:16:29,553
since we started
living here together.

345
00:16:29,684 --> 00:16:32,208
Then I suppose it's time
we settle the score.

346
00:16:32,339 --> 00:16:34,645
- Let's try to relax some.

347
00:16:34,776 --> 00:16:36,169
- [Lu] I'll be white.

348
00:16:36,299 --> 00:16:37,648
- [Hiraku] That means Tia
gets to move first.

349
00:16:37,779 --> 00:16:39,259
- [Lu] Uh... Then I'm black!

350
00:16:39,389 --> 00:16:40,825
- [Hiraku] Fine.

351
00:16:50,487 --> 00:16:53,099
This is definitely a win
for the white team.

352
00:16:55,362 --> 00:16:57,538
- Oh no! My hand just slipped!

353
00:16:57,668 --> 00:17:00,236
- Lu's the type that
likes to hit the reset.

354
00:17:00,367 --> 00:17:01,803
- Sorry about that, Tia.

355
00:17:01,933 --> 00:17:03,283
Since we don't know where
the pieces were,

356
00:17:03,413 --> 00:17:05,067
we'll just need to start over.

357
00:17:05,937 --> 00:17:06,851
[Tia grunts]

358
00:17:06,982 --> 00:17:09,115
What's that look for?

359
00:17:09,245 --> 00:17:10,420
[fingers snap]

360
00:17:16,731 --> 00:17:18,341
[Lu whimpers]

361
00:17:18,472 --> 00:17:21,388
- [Hiraku] Pressing reset
doesn't work against her.

362
00:17:21,518 --> 00:17:22,780
- Don't you find it embarrassing

363
00:17:22,911 --> 00:17:24,304
to use your magic like that?

364
00:17:24,434 --> 00:17:26,306
- Not as embarrassing
as flipping the board

365
00:17:26,436 --> 00:17:29,918
because you think you're
about to lose the game.

366
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,138
You haven't learned
your lesson, have you?

367
00:17:32,268 --> 00:17:34,662
- [Lu] We're playing
the best of three!

368
00:17:34,792 --> 00:17:37,143
- Fine by me,
I accept your challenge.

369
00:17:37,273 --> 00:17:40,189
- [Hiraku] ] It looks nice
and peaceful over there.

370
00:17:44,628 --> 00:17:45,890
[Kuro's paw taps]

371
00:17:46,021 --> 00:17:47,283
- What, here?

372
00:17:48,458 --> 00:17:49,938
Oh, you're absolutely right.

373
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,722
- You're amazing, Kuro.

374
00:17:51,853 --> 00:17:53,724
- He understands the rules?

375
00:17:57,902 --> 00:18:00,035
You're actually playing
the game right.

376
00:18:01,341 --> 00:18:03,560
At a glance, this seems cute,

377
00:18:03,691 --> 00:18:07,912
but I can feel a terrifying
energy coming from them.

378
00:18:11,264 --> 00:18:13,875
I better not challenge
any of them to a game.

379
00:18:14,005 --> 00:18:15,920
- Ah, is your game done?

380
00:18:16,051 --> 00:18:17,835
I'm sure I'm not gonna lose
to the dogs.

381
00:18:17,966 --> 00:18:20,577
- Lu, I don't think
that's a good idea.

382
00:18:20,708 --> 00:18:21,796
- Come on.

383
00:18:21,926 --> 00:18:23,537
What do you say we play a round?

384
00:18:23,667 --> 00:18:25,234
[Lu whimpering]

385
00:18:25,365 --> 00:18:27,018
- [Hiraku] As I expected.

386
00:18:27,149 --> 00:18:30,152
She didn't have the courage
to press the reset button.

387
00:18:32,894 --> 00:18:34,287
Hmm.

388
00:18:36,071 --> 00:18:37,507
- Let's see.

389
00:18:45,211 --> 00:18:47,604
- [Hiraku] Even Kuro shouldn't
be able to fully understand

390
00:18:47,735 --> 00:18:49,128
the game of Majong yet.

391
00:18:49,258 --> 00:18:50,781
It's far too complicated.

392
00:18:50,912 --> 00:18:52,043
- [Lea] This one?

393
00:18:53,610 --> 00:18:55,308
- [Hiraku] It might seem
a little childish,

394
00:18:55,438 --> 00:18:58,311
but I'm going to take
revenge for Lu now.

395
00:18:59,225 --> 00:19:00,226
Riichi!

396
00:19:00,356 --> 00:19:02,402
- [Lea] Ugh, then I call tsumo!

397
00:19:02,532 --> 00:19:03,925
No, wait, I mean ron!

398
00:19:04,055 --> 00:19:05,448
- [Tia] That's ron for me, too.

399
00:19:05,579 --> 00:19:07,842
At least I think so.

400
00:19:07,972 --> 00:19:09,017
- Double ron?

401
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:11,237
Wait, the yasume should save.

402
00:19:11,367 --> 00:19:12,063
Huh?

403
00:19:12,194 --> 00:19:13,761
Me? What?

404
00:19:16,503 --> 00:19:17,460
Are you kidding me right now?

405
00:19:17,591 --> 00:19:19,288
It's the 13 orphans?

406
00:19:19,419 --> 00:19:21,986
- Hey isn't this hand
the one they call yakuman?

407
00:19:22,117 --> 00:19:23,553
- It seemed complicated
at first,

408
00:19:23,684 --> 00:19:26,077
but the game is pretty simple.

409
00:19:26,208 --> 00:19:28,602
- [Lea] Let's see. Hiraku
doesn't have any points left,

410
00:19:28,732 --> 00:19:30,169
so Kuro wins the game.

411
00:19:30,299 --> 00:19:33,911
- Kuro, you're number one.

412
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:45,662
I figured playing only board
games all day wouldn't be good

413
00:19:45,793 --> 00:19:48,970
for our health, so I built
a mini bowling set.

414
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:50,624
- Good luck, Hiraku.

415
00:19:50,754 --> 00:19:53,192
- I'm definitely not just mad
that I lost at Majong.

416
00:19:57,587 --> 00:19:58,545
Come on!

417
00:20:00,590 --> 00:20:02,201
[all gasp]

418
00:20:03,593 --> 00:20:06,509
- Eight pins, not bad.

419
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:08,119
- [Tia] The arsonist
and the serial killer

420
00:20:08,250 --> 00:20:10,165
are really hard to
take down, aren't they?

421
00:20:10,296 --> 00:20:12,863
- [Lea] The scam artist up
front is real tough, too.

422
00:20:12,994 --> 00:20:15,388
- [Hiraku] These nasty sounding
titles are ones we've given

423
00:20:15,518 --> 00:20:17,085
to each of the pins here.

424
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:19,870
They were just normal pins
I'd carved at first, but.

425
00:20:20,001 --> 00:20:21,350
- Why must we hit them?

426
00:20:21,481 --> 00:20:23,134
- Lu hit me with that question.

427
00:20:23,265 --> 00:20:26,921
So I decided the best answer
was to take out the bad guys.

428
00:20:30,664 --> 00:20:31,665
[pins clattering]

429
00:20:31,795 --> 00:20:33,014
Yes!

430
00:20:33,144 --> 00:20:34,711
- I'm up next!

431
00:20:34,842 --> 00:20:36,104
- I don't know if it's

432
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:38,062
because they enjoyed the
simplicity of it,

433
00:20:38,193 --> 00:20:40,674
but the bowling was
a big hit with them.

434
00:20:43,067 --> 00:20:46,375
And so we spent our winter
inside together,

435
00:20:46,506 --> 00:20:49,248
nice and cozy
while playing games.

436
00:20:51,902 --> 00:20:54,992
And those days went by faster
than we thought they would.

437
00:20:55,863 --> 00:20:58,257
[food bubbling]

438
00:21:06,177 --> 00:21:08,745
The snow melted and spring came.

439
00:21:15,012 --> 00:21:16,753
What a lovely morning.

440
00:21:16,884 --> 00:21:20,017
It's gotten nice
and warm outside.

441
00:21:20,148 --> 00:21:22,411
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

442
00:21:25,196 --> 00:21:26,372
- Good morning.

443
00:21:26,502 --> 00:21:28,243
- [Tia] What are we
going to do today?

444
00:21:28,374 --> 00:21:30,158
- There are a few things.

445
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:32,726
I just wanna finish
planting the crop soon.

446
00:21:32,856 --> 00:21:36,904
I think it's time Zabuton
woke up from her hibernation.

447
00:21:37,034 --> 00:21:39,298
We still have some
potatoes, right?

448
00:21:39,428 --> 00:21:41,343
- [Tia] Yes, I believe so.

449
00:21:41,474 --> 00:21:44,346
[hammer tapping]

450
00:21:46,174 --> 00:21:47,697
- Based on the number of taps,

451
00:21:47,828 --> 00:21:50,178
it should be coming
from this direction.

452
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:51,571
- Up there!

453
00:21:54,051 --> 00:21:56,358
- Something big is headed here.

454
00:21:56,489 --> 00:21:58,186
What is that thing?

455
00:21:58,317 --> 00:21:59,753
A dragon?

456
00:21:59,883 --> 00:22:01,320
- No, it's a wyvern!

457
00:22:01,450 --> 00:22:03,365
- It can't be.

458
00:22:03,496 --> 00:22:05,628
[intense music]

459
00:22:08,457 --> 00:22:11,330
[wyvern roars]

460
00:22:17,727 --> 00:22:21,078
["Feel the winds" by
Yui Hizuki plays]

461
00:23:47,774 --> 00:23:50,777
[rustic music playing]

